WEBVTT

00:05.150 --> 00:06.190
<i>You're...</i>

00:06.610 --> 00:07.740
<i>the worst kind of person.</i>

00:10.570 --> 00:11.950
Are you okay?

00:12.410 --> 00:14.330
I'm obviously fine.

00:15.830 --> 00:17.869
Why are you the one crying, Sawaguchi?

00:17.870 --> 00:19.709
I'm the one he hurt.

00:19.710 --> 00:22.960
Because I've never seen
Gou get that mad before...

00:23.800 --> 00:26.259
I also thought he was gonna kill you.

00:26.260 --> 00:27.379
That was scary.

00:27.380 --> 00:30.220
Don't you guys need to go after Gou?

00:32.100 --> 00:34.679
We've never actually
seen Gou get mad before.

00:34.680 --> 00:36.470
We don't know what to do.

00:36.850 --> 00:39.559
Haven't you been friends
with him a long time?

00:39.560 --> 00:41.769
Ever since pre-school.

00:41.770 --> 00:44.979
You're saying Gou's never
been mad in all these years?

00:44.980 --> 00:46.480
Not even once.

00:46.820 --> 00:49.990
Wow. Sounds like a real saint.

00:51.240 --> 00:52.240
Harada.

00:52.740 --> 00:53.740
What?

00:53.741 --> 00:55.449
Go apologize to Gou.

00:55.450 --> 00:55.990
What?

00:55.991 --> 00:58.449
It's not about who was wrong.

00:58.450 --> 01:01.829
But without Gou, who's
going to catch your pitches?

01:01.830 --> 01:03.000
Nobunishi?

01:03.380 --> 01:05.039
Like he could catch for me.

01:05.040 --> 01:07.630
Right? Gou's the only one.

01:08.050 --> 01:11.219
Just go apologize and ask
him to form a battery with you.

01:11.220 --> 01:12.969
I feel the same way.

01:12.970 --> 01:16.890
With the two of you, I know we'll be
able to play some amazing baseball.

01:17.310 --> 01:18.769
What are you talking about?

01:18.770 --> 01:21.059
You play baseball with nine players.

01:21.060 --> 01:23.400
You can't put it on
someone else's shoulders.

01:24.150 --> 01:27.359
But, Harada, it has to
be Gou for you, doesn't it?

01:27.360 --> 01:29.490
In that case, what are you gonna do?

01:33.280 --> 01:34.280
I'm going home.

01:55.090 --> 02:00.640
I've heard it said so many times

02:01.390 --> 02:07.570
How it's not going to work out

02:08.520 --> 02:14.070
That nothing will change

02:14.360 --> 02:20.580
Even if I pretended not to listen

02:21.040 --> 02:24.369
I knew it all

02:24.370 --> 02:27.539
I learned this from you

02:27.540 --> 02:35.540
That it's not a failure, even when it is

02:36.930 --> 02:43.519
When I thrust my feelings
on to the drifting clouds

02:43.520 --> 02:50.439
The quiet melodies push me forward

02:50.440 --> 02:56.949
Because the sky is so vast and free

02:56.950 --> 03:04.580
I decided that I wouldn't cry anymore

03:16.130 --> 03:17.590
Oh, is that you, Takumi?

03:18.430 --> 03:20.810
You look real tired.

03:21.100 --> 03:24.310
Today was my first day of
practice with the baseball team.

03:24.890 --> 03:26.810
And you got tired from just that?

03:28.860 --> 03:30.899
I don't know what to make of you.

03:30.900 --> 03:31.900
Huh?

03:32.780 --> 03:39.910
Normally, you'd say something like how you'd
never get tired from mere baseball practice.

03:46.120 --> 03:47.330
A lover's quarrel?

03:49.000 --> 03:50.919
You had a fight with Gou, didn't you?

03:50.920 --> 03:53.879
You and your wife really went at it.

03:53.880 --> 03:55.090
What are you talking about?

03:55.380 --> 03:57.840
Your neck is red.

03:58.550 --> 04:02.640
Make sure to hide it if you don't
want your mom on your case about it.

04:04.430 --> 04:05.430
Grandpa.

04:06.520 --> 04:11.980
Can someone really tell how much you've
practiced just from feeling your body?

04:13.940 --> 04:15.229
No.

04:15.230 --> 04:16.230
Really?

04:16.320 --> 04:18.110
But today at school...

04:19.030 --> 04:22.490
You've practiced pretty
diligently, haven't you?

04:22.870 --> 04:27.209
Some coaches might be
able to bluff to a certain extent.

04:27.210 --> 04:29.499
No way. I mean, he got it exactly right.

04:29.500 --> 04:30.959
He's bluffing.

04:30.960 --> 04:36.629
If you think junior high kids are
that easy to figure out, you're wrong.

04:36.630 --> 04:38.010
Was he a young guy?

04:38.670 --> 04:40.179
I'm not sure.

04:40.180 --> 04:41.889
Maybe in his thirties.

04:41.890 --> 04:45.309
That's when you get comfortable as a coach.

04:45.310 --> 04:48.979
They feel like they know
everything about kids.

04:48.980 --> 04:51.149
They stop being scared.

04:51.150 --> 04:51.770
What?

04:51.771 --> 04:55.569
Kids that age are the biggest mystery.

04:55.570 --> 04:58.189
Someone who wasn't on my radar

04:58.190 --> 05:04.739
suddenly hit three homers in one game just
'cause a girl he liked came to see the game.

05:04.740 --> 05:10.249
When you just put some label on kids,
you'll usually pay for it later.

05:10.250 --> 05:13.079
That's what kids your age are like.

05:13.080 --> 05:14.630
It's real scary.

05:15.290 --> 05:19.129
So, what's the name of this coach of yours?

05:19.130 --> 05:20.549
His name's Tomura.

05:20.550 --> 05:22.799
Tomura? Makoto?

05:22.800 --> 05:24.259
I don't know.

05:24.260 --> 05:26.139
Do you know a Tomura Makoto?

05:26.140 --> 05:31.979
Yeah. He was a junior starter around
the time I quit coaching for Nitta High.

05:31.980 --> 05:34.520
He was a good kid with talent.

05:34.940 --> 05:36.319
You're thinking of someone else.

05:36.320 --> 05:38.649
This guy's real conniving.

05:38.650 --> 05:41.149
He nags about every little thing.

05:41.150 --> 05:44.909
Saying stuff that has nothing to
do with baseball like hair length.

05:44.910 --> 05:46.199
That's unusual.

05:46.200 --> 05:47.540
What is?

05:48.120 --> 05:52.869
While you never compliment people,
you don't say anything bad either.

05:52.870 --> 05:55.170
But today, that's all you can do.

05:55.750 --> 05:57.250
It's unusual is all.

06:14.770 --> 06:16.310
Are you okay?

06:18.020 --> 06:19.020
What do you mean?

06:19.900 --> 06:21.860
You had a fight with Gou, didn't you?

06:24.450 --> 06:26.450
Who told you that?

06:26.990 --> 06:28.619
Nobody did. I could just tell.

06:28.620 --> 06:30.200
It's because you seem sad.

06:30.660 --> 06:33.460
I'm just not always
laughing foolishly like you.

06:34.080 --> 06:36.329
But you really do seem sad.

06:36.330 --> 06:38.960
It's clear that you must've
had a fight with Gou.

06:39.800 --> 06:42.470
Are you okay? Do you feel hurt?

06:51.220 --> 06:51.890
One, two.

06:51.890 --> 06:52.600
Oh, yeah.

06:52.600 --> 06:53.350
One, two.

06:53.350 --> 06:53.890
Oh, yeah.

06:53.890 --> 06:54.730
One, two.

06:54.730 --> 06:55.440
Oh, yeah.

06:55.440 --> 06:56.230
One, two.

06:56.230 --> 06:56.850
Oh, yeah.

06:56.850 --> 06:57.610
One, two.

06:57.611 --> 07:01.779
Hey, Harada. Gou hasn't talked all day.

07:01.780 --> 07:03.240
Not to you either?

07:03.530 --> 07:06.029
He was just looking really sullen.

07:06.030 --> 07:10.239
When I said that we had nothing
to do with it, he told me to shut up.

07:10.240 --> 07:12.240
He was like a sulky brat.

07:12.750 --> 07:13.750
That right?

07:14.250 --> 07:18.749
I think Gou doesn't know
what to do after he's mad.

07:18.750 --> 07:22.299
Please, could you try to
bury the hatchet with him?

07:22.300 --> 07:25.090
Don't talk when you run.
You'll have trouble breathing.

07:34.890 --> 07:36.479
All right.

07:36.480 --> 07:39.609
It's starting to rain,
so let's call it a day.

07:39.610 --> 07:40.480
What?

07:40.481 --> 07:43.069
Do you have a problem with that, Harada?

07:43.070 --> 07:44.399
We're just ending practice?

07:44.400 --> 07:46.489
Yes, we're done. It's started to rain.

07:46.490 --> 07:49.239
But it's hardly even raining.

07:49.240 --> 07:50.990
They wouldn't even cancel a game.

07:52.700 --> 07:56.249
It's over when we say it's over.

07:56.250 --> 07:58.039
Coach isn't here today.

07:58.040 --> 08:00.419
You're a freshman. Just do as you're told.

08:00.420 --> 08:04.049
Freshman and juniors,
make sure to clean up the equipment.

08:04.050 --> 08:04.760
Dismissed!

08:04.761 --> 08:06.920
Thank you.

08:09.300 --> 08:11.049
Harada.

08:11.050 --> 08:14.679
Are you looking to go
professional or something?

08:14.680 --> 08:17.519
I really wish you'd stop
getting carried away.

08:17.520 --> 08:19.689
Teamwork is very important.

08:19.690 --> 08:22.269
We can't have any outliers.

08:22.270 --> 08:25.399
What are you going to do
when it rains during a game?

08:25.400 --> 08:26.739
What did you say?

08:26.740 --> 08:30.280
We'd still have to play in this
weather, so shouldn't we practice?

08:31.280 --> 08:32.530
I don't think we should.

08:33.530 --> 08:38.119
Our baseball team takes care
that we don't do anything stupid

08:38.120 --> 08:42.539
like try to tough out practice
in the rain and get pneumonia.

08:42.540 --> 08:46.550
You'd do well to fall in line.

08:47.550 --> 08:49.550
Seriously, don't get cocky.

08:52.050 --> 08:56.310
I don't think that's the right attitude
when your elder is talking to you.

09:03.360 --> 09:08.439
Hey, didn't Mr. Tomura
tell you to get your hair cut?

09:08.440 --> 09:13.450
Oh, it's fine. A cute guy like Harada
wouldn't look good with a buzz cut.

09:14.910 --> 09:16.700
Excuse me, Vice Captain.

09:18.330 --> 09:20.499
Could I have the key to the equipment room?

09:20.500 --> 09:22.210
It's locked.

09:28.210 --> 09:29.760
I'll put these away.

09:31.840 --> 09:33.470
Let's go, Takumi.

09:46.480 --> 09:47.480
Gou.

09:48.070 --> 09:50.949
If you're going to come
save me, do it quicker.

09:50.950 --> 09:52.659
Did you want me to save you?

09:52.660 --> 09:53.859
Of course not.

09:53.860 --> 09:55.490
Then what does it matter?

09:57.490 --> 09:59.750
You gotta be more careful.

10:01.250 --> 10:05.540
It's what I thought when you
first started talking to them.

10:06.460 --> 10:08.500
I mean, it's just my observation.

10:09.130 --> 10:10.919
They're pathetic.

10:10.920 --> 10:14.510
They just nag at you
without doing anything.

10:15.300 --> 10:17.510
So if I didn't step in to stop you,

10:18.180 --> 10:20.640
you would've thrown the first punch?

10:23.230 --> 10:26.559
You'll get expelled if you're not careful.

10:26.560 --> 10:28.149
How am I supposed to do that?

10:28.150 --> 10:30.229
Just do what you're told.

10:30.230 --> 10:32.899
You don't have to get your way every time.

10:32.900 --> 10:37.410
Being able to listen to the coach
and your elders is important too.

10:40.410 --> 10:42.499
If it's important, I'll listen.

10:42.500 --> 10:45.289
But I'm never going to shut
up and do what they tell me.

10:45.290 --> 10:46.629
Takumi.

10:46.630 --> 10:47.630
What?

10:48.290 --> 10:50.130
You're on your own, then.

10:50.840 --> 10:51.840
Gou.

10:52.840 --> 10:54.549
Let's play catch.

10:54.550 --> 10:55.969
In the rain?

10:55.970 --> 10:57.549
This is nothing.

10:57.550 --> 10:59.930
We can't let practice just end like this.

11:00.350 --> 11:02.020
I want to pitch.

11:06.690 --> 11:08.769
Sorry, but I just don't feel like it.

11:08.770 --> 11:09.770
Huh?

11:10.070 --> 11:12.109
You're the one who wants to pitch.

11:12.110 --> 11:13.859
You're feeling frustrated, right?

11:13.860 --> 11:17.530
But I'm not here just to entertain you.

11:18.740 --> 11:20.200
You're amazing.

11:20.700 --> 11:24.790
But it doesn't mean I'll always
do everything you tell me to.

11:25.750 --> 11:28.210
You're the one who said you hated that.

11:28.750 --> 11:30.209
Well, I don't like it either.

11:30.210 --> 11:32.590
There's no way I'm letting
you just boss me around.

11:33.630 --> 11:35.130
Or, Takumi...

11:39.010 --> 11:40.350
What is it? Spit it out.

11:41.100 --> 11:45.309
Never mind. I don't know
what I want to say either.

11:45.310 --> 11:47.349
Everything's getting mixed up in my head.

11:47.350 --> 11:48.690
I don't care anymore.

12:04.250 --> 12:06.250
Harada, Otomurai wants to talk to you.

12:06.660 --> 12:07.660
Okay.

12:08.750 --> 12:12.500
Starting today, we'll be doing
some more practical drills.

12:12.920 --> 12:16.259
Practice will follow the schedule.

12:16.260 --> 12:17.419
Yes, sir.

12:17.420 --> 12:19.010
Now, Harada.

12:21.760 --> 12:24.769
Are you planning on quitting the team?

12:24.770 --> 12:27.769
I have no such plans.

12:27.770 --> 12:29.770
Then what's with this hair?

12:30.060 --> 12:32.729
Did you forget what I said two days ago?

12:32.730 --> 12:35.530
Why didn't you do as you're told?

12:39.450 --> 12:41.159
I won't let you play in a game.

12:41.160 --> 12:42.279
Why not?!

12:42.280 --> 12:46.410
How could I put you in an official game
when you can't even listen to your coach?

12:46.750 --> 12:51.670
Look, you may have the talent,
but you don't do what I tell you to.

12:52.130 --> 12:55.420
If you do, I'll cultivate
that talent of yours.

12:56.380 --> 12:57.380
Coach.

12:57.510 --> 13:00.219
Nagakura, I didn't ask for you.

13:00.220 --> 13:02.339
Just follow the practice given to you.

13:02.340 --> 13:07.520
We can't start our calisthenics or
drills until you give Takumi back to us.

13:08.350 --> 13:12.690
You two make quite the pair.

13:13.230 --> 13:16.690
But I'm not putting either
of you in a game, got it?

13:18.440 --> 13:20.399
Hair's got nothing to do with baseball!

13:20.400 --> 13:22.699
Will I pitch faster if I shave my head?!

13:22.700 --> 13:23.990
That's just stupid!

13:26.910 --> 13:28.330
Idiot! You went too far!

13:32.540 --> 13:33.830
Coach.

13:34.250 --> 13:36.419
Maybe you could try batting, then.

13:36.420 --> 13:37.590
What?!

13:39.840 --> 13:44.049
I mean, Harada's pitches really are fast.

13:44.050 --> 13:46.560
I thought maybe you could see for yourself.

13:47.310 --> 13:49.640
I'm sorry, sir.

13:51.440 --> 13:55.610
If the captain himself insists,
I'm willing to see it with my own eyes.

13:55.900 --> 13:57.569
Put the starters in to field.

13:57.570 --> 13:58.860
Coach, you can't!

13:59.150 --> 14:00.359
Why can't I?

14:00.360 --> 14:02.399
Our practice schedule will be ruined.

14:02.400 --> 14:04.199
This won't take long.

14:04.200 --> 14:05.700
Or, Nobunishi...

14:06.370 --> 14:09.080
You got a problem with
how I run things too?

14:10.620 --> 14:11.710
No, sir.

14:12.710 --> 14:15.499
Then you and Midorikawa can sit and watch.

14:15.500 --> 14:17.960
We'll have this precious kid on the mound.

14:18.880 --> 14:20.589
Coach...

14:20.590 --> 14:24.339
Might as well see what
this freshman battery can do.

14:24.340 --> 14:25.890
Thank you!

14:30.100 --> 14:32.519
Otomurai's a pretty good guy.

14:32.520 --> 14:35.019
He let us form a battery.

14:35.020 --> 14:38.149
He at least knows that
Nobunishi can't catch my pitches.

14:38.150 --> 14:40.229
Are you going to pitch against Otomurai?

14:40.230 --> 14:43.240
It's all thanks to Kaionji.

14:50.410 --> 14:51.500
Play ball!

15:01.630 --> 15:02.630
Ball!

15:03.340 --> 15:06.510
Nagakura, did he pitch it
outside on purpose there?

15:07.720 --> 15:08.720
Yes, sir.

15:08.970 --> 15:12.139
So you asked him to bait me, huh?

15:12.140 --> 15:13.140
Yes, sir.

15:23.070 --> 15:24.530
Strike.

15:27.320 --> 15:29.530
He doesn't have a big attitude for nothing.

15:42.170 --> 15:43.170
Yes.

15:48.430 --> 15:49.679
Foul.

15:49.680 --> 15:50.849
Wasn't it?

15:50.850 --> 15:53.219
You're the umpire. You should know.

15:53.220 --> 15:56.519
Was that your call too, Nagakura?

15:56.520 --> 15:57.310
Yes, sir.

15:57.311 --> 16:00.019
No matter how good Harada's control is,

16:00.020 --> 16:03.899
if the batter knows where the pitch is going,
he'll hit it regardless of how fast it's thrown.

16:03.900 --> 16:04.900
Got it?

16:05.400 --> 16:06.949
But it was a foul ball.

16:06.950 --> 16:09.619
You were going for a home run, weren't you?

16:09.620 --> 16:11.160
Yet you swung a little late.

16:11.830 --> 16:13.830
Takumi's pitch didn't lose.

16:14.950 --> 16:16.829
That's not the issue here.

16:16.830 --> 16:20.329
It's the battery's
responsibility if a pitch gets hit.

16:20.330 --> 16:21.629
Harada, come here.

16:21.630 --> 16:23.340
Nobunishi and Midorikawa too.

16:24.250 --> 16:25.340
Listen carefully.

16:26.090 --> 16:31.090
Starting today, Harada and Nagakura will
incorporate pitching after their basic practice.

16:32.510 --> 16:34.720
Are you going to let Harada play in a game?

16:35.100 --> 16:38.100
I'll decide that when the time comes.

16:39.190 --> 16:40.190
Yes, sir.

16:41.310 --> 16:43.769
All right, let's get back to practice.

16:43.770 --> 16:45.899
Midorikawa, you're pitching.

16:45.900 --> 16:48.989
Freshmen, get back to your calisthenics.

16:48.990 --> 16:49.700
Yes, sir.

16:49.701 --> 16:51.740
I have some other business right now.

17:01.750 --> 17:02.790
Hello!

17:05.170 --> 17:06.509
Hello there.

17:06.510 --> 17:08.879
Do you live here?

17:08.880 --> 17:09.720
Yes.

17:09.721 --> 17:11.679
Who are you here to see?

17:11.680 --> 17:12.390
Uh...

17:12.391 --> 17:14.760
Oh, let me guess!

17:19.390 --> 17:22.150
Is it my grandpa?

17:22.480 --> 17:23.899
Yes.

17:23.900 --> 17:25.400
How did you know?

17:25.770 --> 17:27.689
Grandpa's heating the bath.

17:27.690 --> 17:29.649
At this hour?

17:29.650 --> 17:30.610
Yeah.

17:30.611 --> 17:32.859
Dad's coming home from
his business trip tonight.

17:32.860 --> 17:34.159
Do you want to take a bath too?

17:34.160 --> 17:35.989
No, that's all right.

17:35.990 --> 17:37.619
Because you didn't bring spare underwear?

17:37.620 --> 17:39.080
Huh? Yeah.

17:41.040 --> 17:43.170
Grandpa, you have a guest.

17:47.380 --> 17:48.380
Coach.

17:48.960 --> 17:50.509
It's been a long time.

17:50.510 --> 17:52.180
You may not remember me.

17:52.510 --> 17:53.840
Is that you, Makoto?

17:54.470 --> 17:56.179
Have you been well?

17:56.180 --> 17:57.259
Yes.

17:57.260 --> 18:00.680
Actually, there's something
I wanted to talk to you about.

18:01.730 --> 18:03.479
About Takumi, huh?

18:03.480 --> 18:05.939
You seem to see through everything.

18:05.940 --> 18:08.609
Coach, let me just say this directly:

18:08.610 --> 18:10.859
I want to coach Harada.

18:10.860 --> 18:13.160
I want to guide him to his full potential.

18:13.950 --> 18:16.239
But he's too defiant.

18:16.240 --> 18:19.239
It's too hard to coach him
with that personality of his.

18:19.240 --> 18:21.329
So I was hoping you could talk...

18:21.330 --> 18:22.710
Makoto.

18:23.210 --> 18:27.499
Do you go to all your student's
grandfathers and ask for help like this?

18:27.500 --> 18:29.049
Of course not.

18:29.050 --> 18:31.799
I only came because it's you.

18:31.800 --> 18:34.719
I'm sure nobody has more
influence on him than you.

18:34.720 --> 18:37.720
He doesn't get influenced by anyone.

18:39.350 --> 18:45.230
If you came here because you thought Takumi
would listen to me, then you were mistaken.

18:45.850 --> 18:49.729
He's not the type of person
who will listen to anybody.

18:49.730 --> 18:53.740
But maybe that's why he can
pitch the way he does at his age.

18:55.660 --> 18:57.490
Is that a shot at me, Coach?

18:57.870 --> 18:58.910
What?

18:59.700 --> 19:05.369
In high school, we did anything
and everything you told us to.

19:05.370 --> 19:10.460
That's because we believed we could
make it to Koshien if we did as you said.

19:11.420 --> 19:12.260
And?

19:12.261 --> 19:17.469
And I prepared myself
when you stepped down.

19:17.470 --> 19:20.430
That, oh, we can't win anymore.

19:20.720 --> 19:24.770
That you left because you saw
we didn't have the potential to win.

19:25.390 --> 19:29.519
Is that how you saw me quitting?

19:29.520 --> 19:32.319
It's not exactly how I felt.

19:32.320 --> 19:36.949
But when we lost in the fall
tournament, the principal told us

19:36.950 --> 19:40.909
that it makes sense that
Mr. Ioka gave up on us.

19:40.910 --> 19:42.540
That really stung.

19:43.200 --> 19:44.200
You're wrong!

19:45.870 --> 19:50.039
The reason Grandpa quit is
because Grandma got sick.

19:50.040 --> 19:52.709
Grandpa loved Grandma.

19:52.710 --> 19:55.049
He was with her until the very end.

19:55.050 --> 19:59.009
Come on, Seiha. I never
talked to you about that.

19:59.010 --> 20:00.759
You never had to tell me.

20:00.760 --> 20:04.310
Every time you drink, you
always talk about Grandma.

20:05.930 --> 20:07.310
What am I going to do with you?

20:08.150 --> 20:11.819
But you know, that might be as
good as Takumi is going to be.

20:11.820 --> 20:13.399
What are you talking about?!

20:13.400 --> 20:19.070
When I had Harada pitch to me
today, I honestly got goosebumps!

20:19.360 --> 20:23.739
Really? Well, I'm glad you met
a kid that gives you goosebumps.

20:23.740 --> 20:28.330
But to be honest, I wouldn't get
goosebumps from watching Takumi.

20:29.620 --> 20:31.629
That's a pretty awful thing to say.

20:31.630 --> 20:33.339
He's your own grandson.

20:33.340 --> 20:34.669
You might be right.

20:34.670 --> 20:39.259
I'm happy if you think Takumi
still has potential to grow.

20:39.260 --> 20:42.350
Just please don't turn him into
a robot that only wants to win.

20:45.640 --> 20:50.980
Teach him just how fun baseball is to play.

20:52.770 --> 20:54.439
This is awesome.

20:54.440 --> 20:56.149
We might be able to actually play.

20:56.150 --> 20:57.279
Of course.

20:57.280 --> 20:58.899
What are you talking about?

20:58.900 --> 21:01.529
Otomurai is wondering
whether or not to use you.

21:01.530 --> 21:02.989
That's really something.

21:02.990 --> 21:04.949
Remember what I told you?

21:04.950 --> 21:08.330
You don't let someone put
you in games, you just play.

21:09.540 --> 21:11.210
This is our baseball.

21:27.270 --> 21:31.815
I saw you running after
a sparkling white ball

21:31.816 --> 21:36.359
I saw you running after
a sparkling white ball

21:36.360 --> 21:41.845
As it followed a parabola,
disappearing into distant memories

21:41.846 --> 21:47.330
As it followed a parabola,
disappearing into distant memories

21:49.910 --> 21:54.415
You looked back as you
chased after it from afar

21:54.416 --> 21:58.919
You looked back as you
chased after it from afar

21:58.920 --> 22:03.905
The cheers in the stadium echo in my dreams

22:03.906 --> 22:08.889
The cheers in the stadium echo in my dreams

22:08.890 --> 22:13.375
I continue to call out your
name, ever since that fun day

22:13.376 --> 22:17.859
I continue to call out your
name, ever since that fun day

22:17.860 --> 22:19.320
- I love you
- I love you

22:19.323 --> 22:23.050
That was probably the day before eternity

22:23.051 --> 22:26.779
That was probably the day before eternity

22:26.780 --> 22:29.075
If spring comes tomorrow

22:29.076 --> 22:31.369
If spring comes tomorrow

22:31.370 --> 22:33.750
I will go to meet you

22:33.751 --> 22:36.129
I will go to meet you

22:36.130 --> 22:38.360
When the rain turns to sunshine

22:38.361 --> 22:40.589
When the rain turns to sunshine

22:40.590 --> 22:42.885
Will you remember where to stop?

22:42.886 --> 22:45.180
Will you remember where to stop?

22:56.950 --> 22:58.409
<i>You should take a shower.</i>

22:58.410 --> 22:59.910
<i>I'll show you where it is.</i>

23:01.870 --> 23:03.710
<i>This barely fits me.</i>

23:06.250 --> 23:07.920
<i>Here. Eat up.</i>

23:10.840 --> 23:12.130
<i>You really are...</i>

23:13.340 --> 23:14.719
<i>How do I put this?</i>

23:14.720 --> 23:16.469
<i>You think of everything.</i>

23:16.470 --> 23:17.470
<i>You're flawless.</i>

23:20.100 --> 23:21.980
<i>Could I get some more tea?</i>

23:22.350 --> 23:23.600
Make it hot!

